  "hindi": "होता के कार्य के पश्चात् प्रसन्नता के अनुसार रस का आनन्द ले; हे अध्वर्युओ, वह पूर्ण आसेचन चाहता है। उसके लिए इसे लाओ; उसकी कामना करने वाला दाता है। हे धन देने वाले, होता के कार्य से ऋतुओं के साथ सोम पी।",
  "english": "Rejoice, after the Hotṛ's office, at pleasure in the juice; O Adhvaryu priests, he wants a full pouring. Bring this to him; the one who desires it is a giver. From the Hotṛ's office, O wealth-giver, drink Soma with the seasons.",
  "text_flags": [],
  "notes": "joṣam with anu: 'at pleasure' (to one's liking); alternative 'in accordance with satisfaction'. āsicam: 'pouring in' (ā-√sic), sense of 'full pouring' uncertain. tadvaśaḥ dadiḥ: the two nominatives are read as 'one desiring that' and 'giver'; alternative: 'the giver who desires it'. draviṇodaḥ is an epithet 'wealth-giver'; no deity is identified. ṛtubhiḥ 'with the seasons' is literal (the ritual sense of ṛtu is not applied).",
  "confidence": "medium",
  "type": "verse",
