  "hindi": "तुम्हारे वाहक पुष्ट हों, जिनके द्वारा तू जाता है; हानि न करते हुए, हे वन के स्वामी, दृढ़ हो जा। जुड़कर और स्वागत करके, हे साहसी, तू नेष्टा के कार्य से, हे धन देने वाले, ऋतुओं के साथ सोम पी।",
  "english": "Let your bearers thrive, by which you go; not harming, make yourself firm, O Lord of the Forest. Having joined and having welcomed, O bold one, you, from the Neṣṭṛ's office, O wealth-giver, drink Soma with the seasons.",
  "text_flags": [],
  "notes": "Uncertain: vahnayaḥ 'bearers' (not identified); vīḻayasva (printed vīḻayasvā, lengthened final vowel): 'make yourself firm' is a tentative sense of caus. √vīḍ, 'be strong' or 'hold fast' are alternatives; āyūya and abhigūrya: absolutives whose exact senses ('having joined', 'having welcomed/praised') are tentative. vanaspate is rendered 'Lord of the Forest' per glossary, with no identification.",
